<title>EGYPT: Cairo taxidriver dies at wheel, hits lamppost.</title>
<headline>Cairo taxidriver dies at wheel, hits lamppost.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Cairo schoolboy had a taxi ride to remember on Sunday when the driver slumped over the steering wheel and the taxi rammed into a lamppost in the suburb of Giza, the government newspaper al-Akhbar said on Monday.</p>
<p>The driver, Ibrahim Hanafi Ibrahim, 50, had died at the wheel of a heart attack, it said.</p>
